          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దొంగతనం — doṅgatanaṁ — \"a theft; a burglary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నిన్న రాత్రి మా వీధిలో దొంగతనం జరిగింది. ninna rātri mā vīdhilō doṅgatanaṁ jarigindi. Last night there was a theft in our street."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దొంగ, a thief, with -తనం, the ending that makes a noun of a state or a deed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దొంగతనం (doṅgatanaṁ) is native Dravidian: doṅga, \"a thief\" (DEDR 2982), with the Telugu noun ending -tanaṁ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
